==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Healer CC''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Healer Cat CC''' when obtained from [[Healer Awakens!]] (may be dropped on the first stage but guaranteed on the second stage) and is level 20 and above.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal Form'''===
Evolve this Cat as soon as possible, if planning to use it. Healer, in his original form, has a very inconsistent ability, which, combined with the pathetic health, causes this unit to die very easily, only to not come back until his very long recharge time allows for another to be summoned.

==='''Evolved Form'''===
Even though Healer CC still has very poor health and attack power, his guaranteed freeze ability becomes very useful, as it can be used to permanently stop enemies with slow attack rates, single target or short range, if aided by [[Cat Combo|Combos]] or others with the same ability. Even without such help, if he has a chance to stay alive, he can still provide a lot of help in holding an enemy in place.

==='''True Form'''===
Healer Cat CC, with his new ability, Area Attack, basically serves as a [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]] or [[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|iCat]] for all non-Metal enemies, but with much more limited use due to pathetic range and mainly recharge time. Because of this, Healer Cat CC can be used to [[cheese]] a few levels ([[Heavenly Tower/Floor 30|Floor 30]], [[Heavenly Tower/Floor 40|Floor 40]], [[Heavenly Tower/Floor 50|Floor 50]], [[Flow Like the Stream (Merciless)|Flow Like The Stream]], [[Puffer Planet (Merciless)|Puffer Planet]], [[Flappy Cat (Insane)|Flappy Cat]], [[Forest Beasts (Deadly)|Forest Beasts]], [[Tiny Wings (Deadly)|Tiny Wings]], [[The Red Cat Gambit]], [[The Holy Exploit]]) by exploiting the enemy limit, long attack rates, or the short range of certain enemies.

It takes one Freeze up (S) and one Freeze up (M) in order to perma-freeze the enemies he targets with a single Healer Cat, provided you have all Fruit Treasures; thus, [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]], [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] and [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]] enemies cannot be perma-frozen with just him alone. However, Healer Cat CC still can work extremely well against isolated Traitless bosses, provided you also have the support of [[Lone Cat and Kitten (Rare Cat)|Tourist Cat]], which is key as they cover each other's downtime.

